From 866bcf3d91e94dc94dec9c5e0867d02a330ddde0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:42:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: the press that wakes the camera from Standby does nothing
 else

Why: in Standby a button press dispatched wake and returned, but the
input class never learned of it: its gesture counter kept counting
that press. A Hold mapped to standby put the camera back to sleep
3 s after it woke, and a double click woke it and then took a photo.
Original Apertar consumes a wake press: the power button's callback
returns bool and on true the gesture is consumed ("A wake press cannot
seed another sleep.", StandbyPowerButtonInput.cpp:66-71 at
upstream-1.6.0), and buttons fire on press only, so a wake press has
no follow-up (conventions HW-5).

What: ButtonGesture gets consume(): the press so far gives no click,
long press or Hold. The GPIO, PCF8574 and NeoRotary button callbacks
return bool (PressCallback; rotation and Listen callbacks stay void),
emitAction returns the callback's answer, and on true the button's
gesture is consumed. handleHardwareInputAction returns true exactly
when it dispatched wake. Switches ignore the answer and behave as
before; test_input and the power button ignore it too.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the 18 host tests pass. Scratch
ButtonGesture program: press, consume, release in 200 ms -> no Single;
press, consume, held 3.1 s -> no Hold; the next press fires Press. A
scratch program drove GpioInput and Pcf8574Input through an LD_PRELOAD
fake of the chip and /dev/i2c-1 with a callback that wakes on the
first press: before, a 3.5 s hold gave wake then standby and a double
click gave wake, record_toggle, photo; now wake only, and wake,
record_toggle (the second press is a new press, as in 1.6.0).
--simulate: enter_standby, test_input gpio_buttons d17 wakes only with
the same reply; smoke_core.sh shapes keep every 1.6.0 field. Needs the
camera: d17=record_toggle, d17_hold=standby, d17_double=photo; enter
Standby, hold d17 3 s: journalctl -u apertar-core -f shows one wake and
no enter_standby; enter Standby, double-click d17: it wakes and no new
photo appears (a take may start from the second press; stop it). Same
with a NeoRotary push and a PCF8574 pin.

